From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:10:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: restore the baseband multipliers to
 the right slots

Each core's baseband multiplier lives in table 13 at 0x63 + 4 * core,
with a copy at 0x73 + 4 * core; b43_phy_ht_tx_power_fix() writes both.
b43_phy_ht_stop_playback() restored the copy to 0x67 + 4 * core
instead, overwriting core 1's multiplier with core 0's and core 2's
with core 1's.

At the moment this only happens around the idle TSSI measurement during
init, and the channel switch that follows rewrites the multipliers, so
the damage is short-lived; it would not be with any later use of tone
playback (e.g. calibration).

Fixes: 371ec465a358 ("b43: HT-PHY: implement stopping sample tone playback")
Signed-off-by: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
index 57f80093e9d1..b259fefc3826 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@ static void b43_phy_ht_stop_playback(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 		if (phy_ht->bb_mult_save[i] >= 0) {
 			b43_httab_write(dev, B43_HTTAB16(13, 0x63 + i * 4),
 					phy_ht->bb_mult_save[i]);
-			b43_httab_write(dev, B43_HTTAB16(13, 0x67 + i * 4),
+			b43_httab_write(dev, B43_HTTAB16(13, 0x73 + i * 4),
 					phy_ht->bb_mult_save[i]);
 		}
 	}
